From 467d95930e5cf67f5c902c4a609d66490581c2a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <fardjad.davari2@jumbo.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:15:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add swarm-scoped hook context and post-tool transforms

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: propagate swarm context to lifecycle hooks and add post-tool result transforms
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: upstream-candidate
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: none
X-Jcode-Patch-File: 0002-candidate-add-hook-context-and-post-tool-transform.patch

Patch intent:
Add a swarm context system that scopes hook invocations to the correct
process role (coordinator, worker, or internal) and swarm-enabled state.
Wrap the complete non-streaming run_once body in swarm context so upstream
lifecycle hooks retain the selected role.
Add synchronous post_tool_transform hooks that receive tool input and result
JSON on stdin, with large payloads spilled to temp files. Propagate the swarm
context into spawned tool-execution tasks so transformer hooks always see the
correct coordinator or worker identity.
The transform runs before upstream's post_tool_feedback hook, so feedback
is appended to the transformed result rather than discarded by a replacement.

Why it exists:
Post-tool transformers need swarm metadata to decide whether to act (e.g., the
delegation guard only replaces oversized coordinator results, preserving worker
and internal output). Without explicit propagation, tokio::spawn lost the
task-local swarm context, causing hooks to fall back to Internal with swarm
disabled. The generic context exposes process role, worker identity, and swarm
state without personal worker blueprints.

Upstream integration points:
crates/jcode-base/src/hooks.rs (SwarmContext, ProcessRole, with_swarm_context,
current_swarm_context, transform_tool_result, hook_configured), crates/jcode-app-core/
src/tool/mod.rs (Registry::execute transform invocation),
src/agent.rs (per-session swarm state),
src/agent/turn_execution.rs (run_once, run_once_streaming,
current_swarm_hook_context),
crates/jcode-app-core/src/agent/turn_streaming_mpsc.rs (tokio::spawn tool
execution context propagation), crates/jcode-app-core/src/server/swarm.rs
(run_swarm_task worker context),
crates/jcode-config-types/src/lib.rs (HooksConfig fields, alongside upstream
post_tool_feedback and its timeout),
crates/jcode-base/src/config/default_file.rs,
crates/jcode-base/src/config/env_overrides.rs, docs/HOOKS.md.

Update guidance:
Keep the non-streaming run_once body inside with_swarm_context so upstream
turn_start and turn_end hooks inherit the session scope. Keep the streaming
scope around the complete lifecycle, including start and end hooks. The spawned
tool-execution task in turn_streaming_mpsc.rs must capture the swarm context
before tokio::spawn and re-scope it inside the spawned task with
with_swarm_context. Worker execution must install its explicit worker context
before calling the agent, and coordinator fallback must derive role from the
session and feature state. Preserve task isolation when changing hook dispatch.
The post_tool_transform hook is synchronous and must fail open: any error or
timeout leaves the original result unchanged. Keep transform-then-feedback
ordering in Registry::execute and reuse upstream's fire_post_tool_hook(input)
signature.

Validation:
cargo test -p jcode-app-core --lib -- agent_turn_hook_context_tracks_coordinator_swarm_feature
cargo test -p jcode-app-core --lib -- agent_turn_hook_context_preserves_explicit_worker_scope
cargo test -p jcode-app-core --lib -- registry_execute_post_tool_transform_replaces_model_visible_result
cargo test -p jcode-app-core --lib -- registry_execute_post_tool_transform_fails_open_for_all_failure_modes
cargo test -p jcode-app-core --lib -- post_tool_feedback_appends_after_post_tool_transform
cargo test -p jcode-base --lib -- swarm_context_propagates_into_spawned_task
cargo test -p jcode-base --lib -- swarm_context_lost_without_explicit_propagation_in_spawned_task
cargo test -p jcode-base --lib -- swarm_context_defaults_to_internal
cargo test -p jcode-base --lib -- swarm_context_is_scoped_to_async_future
cargo test -p jcode-app-core run_subagent_hook_context --lib
cargo test -p jcode-app-core --lib -- run_once_preserves_swarm_context_during_turn_execution
